Too bad, it is more nearly far from functioning -- in the sense of being used 
freely for communication on all manner of topics -- than it is not fully 
defined.  While that is perhaps technically correct, the definition of Lojban is 
so much more nearly complete that that of any other language -- Esperanto very 
definitely included, it being worse off than, say, English, for want of serious 
studies -- that bringing that in as objections is fairly ludicrous.  There may 
be problems with Lojban (oy, may there be) but underdefinition is certainly not 
one of them.




________________________________
